### Apply NameResolver Visitor to AST

Source: https://github.com/nikic/php-parser/blob/master/doc/component/Name_resolution.markdown

Use the NameResolver visitor to resolve names within an Abstract Syntax Tree (AST). This is the recommended approach for most AST uses.

```php
$nameResolver = new PhpParser\NodeVisitor\NameResolver;
$nodeTraverser = new PhpParser\NodeTraverser;
$nodeTraverser->addVisitor($nameResolver);

// Resolve names
$stmts = $nodeTraverser->traverse($stmts);
```

--------------------------------

### Encode AST to JSON

Source: https://github.com/nikic/php-parser/blob/master/doc/component/JSON_representation.markdown

Use `json_encode()` to serialize the AST into a JSON string. This method requires the AST nodes to implement the `JsonSerializable` interface. The output includes attributes and comments.

```php
<?php

use PhpParser\ParserFactory;

$code = <<<'CODE'
<?php

/** @param string $msg */
function printLine($msg) {
    echo $msg, "\n";
}
CODE;

$parser = (new ParserFactory())->createForHostVersion();

try {
    $stmts = $parser->parse($code);

    echo json_encode($stmts, JSON_PRETTY_PRINT), "\n";
} catch (PhpParser\Error $e) {
    echo 'Parse Error: ', $e->getMessage();
}

```

--------------------------------

### Decode JSON to AST

Source: https://github.com/nikic/php-parser/blob/master/doc/component/JSON_representation.markdown

Use `JsonDecoder::decode()` to convert a JSON string back into an AST. This is useful for reconstructing ASTs from serialized data.

```php
<?php

$jsonDecoder = new PhpParser\JsonDecoder();
$ast = $jsonDecoder->decode($json);

```

### Introduction > What else can it do?

Source: https://github.com/nikic/php-parser/blob/master/doc/0_Introduction.markdown

Beyond parsing, the package includes support for pretty printing (converting AST to PHP code), serializing/unserializing the node tree to JSON, dumping the node tree in a human-readable format, and infrastructure for traversing and changing the AST using node traversers and visitors, including a visitor for resolving namespaced names.

--------------------------------

### Usage of basic components > AST traversal > The NameResolver node visitor

Source: https://github.com/nikic/php-parser/blob/master/doc/2_Usage_of_basic_components.markdown

The `NameResolver` node visitor helps in working with namespaced code by resolving names to their fully qualified forms. It tracks aliases and namespaces to determine the correct resolution. After running `NameResolver`, most names become fully qualified, except for unqualified function and constant names which are resolved at runtime. It also adds a `namespacedName` subnode to declarations for namespaced names.

